>>5) What items are ESSENTIAL for finishing the game? (I've Finally got
>>   a shot at it!)
>	The amulet of yendor, staying alive (or at least undead),
>	are all that's really required.  To stay alive (etc) it
>	helps to have speed, various other intrinsics, and the
>	ability (knowledge) to escape or evade the Wizard.  Everything
>	else is subject to debates and flame wars.

The only absolute essentials are the Amulet of Yendor and fire
resistance. However, without using the paralysis trick, it is
impossible to escape or evade the wizard. This is by no means essential
anyway.
Other things which are near essential (in rough order of importance):

  Magic resistance
  AC better than  -10
  A good artifact or at least a decent +6 to +8 weapon
  AC better than  -20
  Teleport control
  Reflection (or at least disintegration resistance)
  Levitation
  Amulet(s) of life saving (particularly if this is your first real
                            attempt at winning)

No flames please. Obviously these will depend on individual
circumstances. If the wizard is on the level below the castle, then
teleport control is quite unnecessary, and if he is on level 50 then
it's essential. If this is your first attempt, I would probably wish
for at least two amulets of life saving ahead of other more useful
things (speed boots, helms of telepathy or brilliance, blessed 
luckstones, etc.....).


